<td id="S4.T1.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T1.2.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overall</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T1.2.6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2,636</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.6.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T1.2.6.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">2,407</span></td>
<td id="S4.T1.2.6.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t"><span id="S4.T1.2.6.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">91.3</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Task Complexity Analysis</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Performance varies significantly by task complexity (Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2 Task Complexity Analysis ‣ 4 Results ‣ MacroBench: A Novel Testbed for Web Automation Scripts via Large Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>). Simple automation tasks (91.7% success) are handled reliably across all models, while
medium-complexity workflows requiring multi-step coordination show degraded performance (84.1%). Complex tasks involving conditional logic, error recovery, and cross-page workflows
remain largely unsolved (0.0% success), highlighting fundamental limitations in current LLMs’ planning and error-handling capabilities.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Performance breakdown by task complexity level.</figcaption>
